What is Child Resistant Packaging?
Child resistant packaging (CRP) comprises containers and closures engineered with mechanisms that impede children from opening them while remaining operable for adults. Typical formats include push and turn caps, blister packs with age appropriate barriers, and tamper evident seals that satisfy regulatory standards such as the U.S. Consumer Product Safety Commission’s Poison Prevention Packaging Act. The primary purpose is to prevent accidental ingestion of medicines, household chemicals, and personal care products by toddlers and young children.
