Key Market Drivers
1. Strengthening Regulatory Frameworks
Governments in North America, Europe, and emerging Asian economies have introduced stricter child safety statutes that mandate compliant packaging for pharmaceuticals, household chemicals, and consumer care products. Compliance has become a decisive factor in supplier selection, prompting manufacturers to invest in advanced molding and testing technologies that meet ASTM and ISO benchmarks.
2. Growing Consumer Awareness and Liability Management
Surveys consistently show that more than 68% of parents consider child resistant features when purchasing over the counter items. This heightened vigilance drives premium pricing for brands that can demonstrably protect young users while also reducing exposure to costly product recall litigation.
